      "created_at": "2024-05-06T11:54:38Z",
      "updated_at": "2024-05-06T11:54:38Z",
      "body": "honestly – no idea. it probably does, but there isn't a ready-made package for react native (yet?)\r\n\r\njudging by their docs, `WebSocket`s are supported, so for transport `WebSocketTransport` from `@mtcute/web` should work fine\r\nas for crypto – `@mtcute/web` uses a mix of wasm-based crypto and webcrypto apis, neither of which are supported by react native...\r\nfor storage mtcute primarily uses sqlite, and react native does seem to have some libraries that provide bindings for those, but i don't know how well would they work with mtcute\r\n\r\ntldr: out of the box – not right now, but i will eventually get to react native too. or you can pass custom crypto/storage implementations (or contribute!) if you are eager :D ",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
